You got a new look and I like that.

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:08.620
New year, new you! Aaaaah...

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:10.160
I always find that slogan annoying because

00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:12.800
you don't get a new you the day it turns to a new year.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:15.120
New you takes a lot of hard work, a-and

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:18.580
that's kind of a discipline thing that I'm committing myself to this year.

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:21.020
I talked about this is in the sixteen million video but,

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:23.960
uh, this year I've been doing a ton of self improvement stuff, I've been

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:26.920
exercising the first thing I do when I wake up.

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.880
I wake up at 7:20am, and then I go work out for an hour,

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:32.880
and then I take a shower, and then I practice guitar for an hour,

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:35.020
and then I learn German for an hour, and then throughout the day

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:39.940
whenever I feel like it, and then I record for about four hours straight and that's every single day.

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:44.000
What I'm- what I'm trying to get at is that you can't have a new you instantly.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:46.520
You can't just automatically do a new you.

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:48.320
You can't wake up one day and say, like,

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:55.180
"I'M DIFFERENT AS OF TODAY AND EVERYONE'S GONNA RECOGNIZE HOW DIFFERENT AND GREAT I'VE BECOME!"

00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:59.220
It's still a lot of work. Motivation is one thing, and I said this on, uh,

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:03.820
on Facebook and Instagram when I was doing my sweat updates, uh, in the morning,

00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:10.980
um, but I said motivation is one thing, but motivation is temporary. Motivation is like a feeling you get that fades away.

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:18.880
The only way to really get change is to commit yourself to discipline. To discipline yourself is to commit to something and make it a habit,

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:23.380
and hold yourself accountable for those changes on a day to day basis.

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:27.720
Doing the same thing every day becomes a habit, but it's harder and harder as time goes on,

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:33.740
because your body resists change. And it doesn't wanna change, it's comfortable where it is, so you have to

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:38.260
hold yourself accountable, and that's where discipline overtakes motivation in a lot of ways.

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:40.740
And that's kinda what I'm holding myself to this year.

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:43.240
I'm not even trying to, like, shove it in people's faces that,

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:48.120
"Hey, look at me, new year, new me! I'm doing a great job at being amazing!"

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:49.820
